From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:30:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST War: retire flag AirRebaseHeal to fit
 ConquestTraitTargets in the 64-bit masks

Build 18386e5 failed: 65 flags (ABTestFixesFitMask). AirRebaseHeal (bug H2)
was off in the bundle and can't show in T150 games (no aircraft); its code
goes, leaving CP's behaviour, as with the lead's retired flags. The bug stays
documented in RESULTS.md (CvHomelandAI audit, H2).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G2NZizcmgfGkXsgJcVcF7h
---
 CvGameCoreDLL_Expansion2/CvHomelandAI.cpp | 6 ------
 CvGameCoreDLL_Expansion2/CvPlayer.cpp     | 2 +-
 CvGameCoreDLL_Expansion2/CvPlayer.h       | 1 -
 3 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CvGameCoreDLL_Expansion2/CvHomelandAI.cpp b/CvGameCoreDLL_Expansion2/CvHomelandAI.cpp
index 47113afbe..b326f9b87 100644
--- a/CvGameCoreDLL_Expansion2/CvHomelandAI.cpp
+++ b/CvGameCoreDLL_Expansion2/CvHomelandAI.cpp
@@ -5715,12 +5715,6 @@ void CvHomelandAI::ExecuteAircraftMoves()
 				if (!pUnit->canRebase() || !(it->pPlot->isCity()))
 					continue;
 
-				//AI_AB_TEST (candidate, flag AirRebaseHeal): the bases are sorted quietest first, so once we reach one no
-				//quieter than our own there is nothing better. CP skips past its own base and rebases to a busier one every
-				//turn, and a plane that rebases never heals.
-				if (m_pPlayer->UsesCandidateAI(FIX_AIR_REBASE_HEAL) && it->score >= scoreLookup[pUnit->plot()->GetPlotIndex()])
-					break;
-
 				//apparently we're already in the best possible base?
 				if (pUnit->plot() == it->pPlot)
 					continue;
